From: hIRoic Linux hammer PoC <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: disable FDPIC code generation for the kernel

An ARM FDPIC userspace toolchain enables -mfdpic by default.  The kernel
is a fixed-address image and must not inherit that userspace ABI: doing so
emits R_ARM_FUNCDESC relocations and can make a normal kernel link depend
on FDPIC dynamic-linker sections.  It also triggers a null-section crash
in the Binutils 2.45.1 ARM backend for this XIP configuration.

Explicitly select the normal kernel code-generation model when the
compiler supports the option.  This is especially important for XIP,
where code addresses are fixed by the linker script.

Upstream-status: Pending
---
 arch/arm/Makefile | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/Makefile b/arch/arm/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/Makefile
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@ GZFLAGS		:=-9
 # Never generate .eh_frame
 KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-option,-fno-dwarf2-cfi-asm)
 
+# A userspace FDPIC toolchain must not apply that ABI to the kernel.
+KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-option,-mno-fdpic)
+
 # This should work on most of the modern platforms
 KBUILD_DEFCONFIG := multi_v7_defconfig
 
-- 
2.47.3
